window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":37,"nomSourate":"As-Saffat","nomFr":"Les rangés","nomEn":"Those who set the Ranks","nomArabe":"الصافات","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":56,"nbVersets":182,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ وَالصَّافَّاتِ صَفًّا","tradPropre":"Par ceux qui sont rangés en rangs.","tradEn":"By those [angels] lined up in rows","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> En adoration devant leur Seigneur, comme le sont les fidèles en prière.","explicationUnanime":"Je prête serment par les anges qui se mettent en rangs serrés durant leur adoration.","explicationEn":"1. I take an oath on the angels who form compact rows in their worship.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-36-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"فَالزَّاجِرَاتِ زَجْرًا","tradPropre":"Par ceux qui poussent (les nuages) avec force.","tradEn":"And those who drive [the clouds]","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les nuages, selon la majorité des exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Je prête serment par les anges qui poussent les nuages vers le lieu où Allah veut qu’il pleuve.","explicationEn":"2. And I also take an oath on the angels who drive the rainclouds and send them to wherever I command they send rain.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"فَالتَّالِيَاتِ ذِكْرًا","tradPropre":"Par ceux qui récitent, en rappel:","tradEn":"And those who recite the message,","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les paroles d’Allah qu’ils transmettent aux Messagers, selon la majorité des commentateurs.","explicationUnanime":"Je prête serment par les anges qui récitent les paroles d’Allah.","explicationEn":"3. And I take an oath in the angels who recite the Qur’ān.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ إِلَاهَكُمْ لَوَاحِدٌ","tradPropre":"«Votre Dieu est en vérité unique,","tradEn":"Indeed, your God is One,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, votre Dieu qui mérite d’être adoré est Un et n’a pas d’associé: c’est Allah.","explicationEn":"4. O people! Indeed, your true deity is one and has no partner: He is Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ الْمَشَارِقِ","tradPropre":"le Seigneur des cieux et de la terre et de ce qui existe entre eux et Seigneur des Levants»","tradEn":"Lord of the heavens and the earth and that between them and Lord of the sunrises.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Et des occidents, précisent certains exégètes. Le soleil se lève en effet, et se couche, en des lieux différents selon les saisons.","explicationUnanime":"Il est le Seigneur des Cieux, de la Terre et de ce qui se trouve entre les deux, le Seigneur du soleil à chaque fois qu’il se lève et qu’il se couche tout au long de l’année.","explicationEn":"5. The lord of the heavens; the lord of the earth; the lord of what is between the two, and the lord of the sun in all its rising and setting places throughout the year.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا زَيَّنَّا السَّمَاءَ الدُّنْيَا بِزِينَةٍ الْكَوَاكِبِ","tradPropre":"Nous avons décoré le ciel le plus proche d'un décor: les étoiles,","tradEn":"Indeed, We have adorned the nearest heaven with an adornment of stars","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons embelli le ciel le plus proche de la Terre d’un bel ornement: ce sont les astres qui paraissent comme des bijoux scintillants.","explicationEn":"6. Indeed, I have beautified the nearest of the heavens to the earth with a beautiful decoration: the stars that are like sparkling jewels to the eyesight.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"وَحِفْظًا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْطَانٍ مَارِدٍ","tradPropre":"afin de le protéger contre tout diable rebelle.","tradEn":"And as protection against every rebellious devil","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons préservé le ciel le plus bas, grâce à ces étoiles qui sont projetées contre tout démon rebelle.","explicationEn":"7. And I have protected the nearest sky from every rebellious satan, who abstains from my obedience, with the shooting stars.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"لَا يَسَّمَّعُونَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ الْأَعْلَىٰ وَيُقْذَفُونَ مِنْ كُلِّ جَانِبٍ","tradPropre":"Ils ne pourront être à l'écoute des dignitaires suprêmes [les Anges]; car ils seront harcelés de tout côté,","tradEn":"[So] they may not listen to the exalted assembly [of angels] and are pelted from every side,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces démons ne peuvent entendre, dans le Ciel, les anges parler de ce que leur a révélé leur Seigneur comme prescriptions religieuses ou comme décret et on lancera sur eux des météores de toute part.","explicationEn":"8. These satans are not able to hear the angels in the heavens, when they discuss the law and decree of Allah they are inspired with. They are bombarded with shooting stars from all sides.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"دُحُورًا  وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ وَاصِبٌ","tradPropre":"et refoulés. Et ils auront un châtiment perpétuel.","tradEn":"Repelled; and for them is a constant punishment,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceci, afin de les chasser et de les empêcher d’écouter les anges. Puis dans l’au-delà, ils subiront un châtiment douloureux et permanent qui ne s’interrompra pas.","explicationEn":"9. To exile them and drive them away from eavesdropping. And in the Hereafter they will suffer a painful, everlasting punishment which will not end.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا مَنْ خَطِفَ الْخَطْفَةَ فَأَتْبَعَهُ شِهَابٌ ثَاقِبٌ","tradPropre":"Sauf celui qui saisit au vol quelque [information]; il est alors pourchassé par un météore transperçant.","tradEn":"Except one who snatches [some words] by theft, but they are pursued by a burning flame, piercing [in brightness].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Excepté le démon qui saisit au vol des mots échangés par les anges et qui ne sont pas encore parvenus aux habitants de la Terre. Un météore brûlant le poursuit alors et les consume, mais il se peut qu’il rapporte à ses frères les mots qu’il a entendus avant que le météore ne le consume et que ces paroles soient transmises à des devins qui profèrent alors cent mensonges à côté de ces mots.","explicationEn":"10. Except for those satans who happen to quickly snatch something; a statement that the angels discuss among themselves which the people of earth have not yet received information of. A shooting star then goes after it and burns it. Sometimes, the satan is able to pass that information on to its companion before it is burnt by the shooting star, and it reaches the fortune-tellers, who tell a hundred lies with it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"فَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ أَهُمْ أَشَدُّ خَلْقًا أَمْ مَنْ خَلَقْنَا  إِنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُمْ مِنْ طِينٍ لَازِبٍ","tradPropre":"Demande-leur s'ils sont plus difficiles à créer que ceux que Nous avons créés? Car Nous les avons créés de boue collante!","tradEn":"Then inquire of them, [O Muḥammad], \"Are they a stronger [or more difficult] creation or those [others] We have created?\" Indeed, We created them [i.e., men] from sticky clay.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Comme les cieux, la terre, les étoiles, les anges et les démons qui viennent d’être mentionnés.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, demande aux mécréants qui rejettent la réalité de la Ressuscitation s’ils sont plus imposants, plus forts et de corpulence plus grande, que ceux que Nous avons créés dans les Cieux et sur la Terre et plus forts que les anges? Nous les avons créés d’une boue collante. Comment peuvent-ils donc rejeter la réalité de la Ressuscitation alors qu’ils sont créés d’une matière vile qui est la boue collante?","explicationEn":"11. O Muhammad! So ask the disbelievers who reject the resurrection: “Are you harder to create, and greater in form than other things that Allah has created from the heavens, the earth and the angels?” Indeed, Allah created them from sticky clay, so how could they deny the resurrection when they were created from such a weak substance?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"بَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Mais tu t'étonnes, et ils se moquent!","tradEn":"But you wonder, while they mock,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, tu t’étonnes plutôt du pouvoir d’Allah et de Sa gestion des affaires de Ses créatures et tu t’étonnes du rejet des polythéistes de toute idée de Ressuscitation. Ces gens-là en sont arrivés à railler ce que tu dis au sujet de la Ressuscitation.","explicationEn":"12. O Muhammad! You are amazed at the power of Allah and His management of the affairs of His creation; you are astonished at the idolaters rejecting the resurrection. While these idolaters mock at what you say regarding the resurrection, due to their extreme denial of it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَإِذَا ذُكِّرُوا لَا يَذْكُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et quand on le leur rappelle (le Coran), ils ne se rappellent pas;","tradEn":"And when they are reminded, they remember not.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu’on exhorte ces polythéistes, ils ne tirent pas profit de l’exhortation à cause de la dureté de leurs cœurs.","explicationEn":"13. If these idolaters were to be advised with any advice, they would not take heed from it and would not benefit, because of their hard-heartedness.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"وَإِذَا رَأَوْا آيَةً يَسْتَسْخِرُونَ","tradPropre":"et quand ils voient un prodige, ils cherchent à s'en moquer,","tradEn":"And when they see a sign, they ridicule.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu’ils voient un des signes de la véracité du Prophète, ils le raillent exagérément et feignent l’étonnement.","explicationEn":"14. And when they witness a miracle from the miracles of the Prophet (peace be upon him) that prove his truthfulness, they exaggerate in showing astonishment and mocking it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا إِنْ هَاذَا إِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"et disent: «Ceci n'est que magie évidente.","tradEn":"And say, \"This is not but obvious magic.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils disent: Ce que Muħammad apporte n’est que sorcellerie manifeste.","explicationEn":"15. And they say, “This thing that Muhammad has brought is nothing but clear sorcery.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"أَإِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَعِظَامًا أَإِنَّا لَمَبْعُوثُونَ","tradPropre":"Lorsque nous serons morts et que nous deviendrons poussière et ossements, serons-nous ressuscités?","tradEn":"When we have died and become dust and bones, are we indeed to be resurrected?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque nous mourrons et que nous nous transformerons en poussière et ossements, retournerons-nous à la vie après cela? Ceci est assurément exclu.","explicationEn":"16. “So when we die and become dust and decomposed, crumbling bones, will we be resurrected alive after that? That is indeed, far-fetched.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"أَوَآبَاؤُنَا الْأَوَّلُونَ","tradPropre":"ainsi que nos premiers ancêtres?»","tradEn":"And our forefathers [as well]?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nos anciens aïeux seront-ils également ressuscités?","explicationEn":"17. “Will our ancient forefathers who dies before us also be resurrected?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"قُلْ نَعَمْ وَأَنْتُمْ دَاخِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Oui! et vous vous humilierez».","tradEn":"Say, \"Yes, and you will be [rendered] contemptible.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, réponds-leur: Oui, vous serez ressuscités après que vous soyez devenus ossements et poussière. De même, vos anciens aïeux seront également ressuscités et tous serez ressuscités, en étant humiliés et contraints.","explicationEn":"18. O Muhammad! Say to them in reply: “Yes, you shall be resurrected after you have turned into dust and decomposed bones, and your forefathers will also be resurrected; you will all be resurrected in the condition that you are in a despised and humiliating state.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"فَإِنَّمَا هِيَ زَجْرَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ فَإِذَا هُمْ يَنْظُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Il n'y aura qu'un seul Cri, et voilà qu'ils regarderont,","tradEn":"It will be only one shout, and at once they will be observing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce n’est que l’affaire d’un souffle dans la Trompe (le second souffle) et tous assisterons alors aux évènements terribles du Jour de la Résurrection, attendant ce qu’Allah fera d’eux.","explicationEn":"19. It will only be one blow of the trumpet (the second blowing), and suddenly they will all be looking at the horrors of the Day of Judgement, awaiting what Allah will do with them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا يَا وَيْلَنَا هَاذَا يَوْمُ الدِّينِ","tradPropre":"et ils diront: «Malheur à nous! c'est le jour de la Rétribution».","tradEn":"They will say, \"O woe to us! This is the Day of Recompense.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les polythéistes qui rejettent la réalité de la Ressuscitation diront: Que notre perte est immense, ceci est le Jour de la Rétribution durant lequel Allah rétribue Ses serviteurs pour ce qu’ils ont fait dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"20. The idolaters who reject the resurrection say, “May we be doomed! This is the Day of Requital on which Allah will requite His servants for whatever deeds they sent forth in their worldly life!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"هَاذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ الَّذِي كُنْتُمْ بِهِ تُكَذِّبُونَ","tradPropre":"«C'est le jour du Jugement que vous traitiez de mensonge».","tradEn":"[They will be told], \"This is the Day of Judgement which you used to deny.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On leur répondra: Ceci est le Jour du Jugement des serviteurs dont vous rejetiez l’existence dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"21. It will be said to them: “This is the Day of Judgement between the servants, which you used to deny and reject in the world!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"۞ احْشُرُوا الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا وَأَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوا يَعْبُدُونَ","tradPropre":"«Rassemblez les injustes et leurs épouses et tout ce qu'ils adoraient,","tradEn":"[The angels will be ordered], \"Gather those who committed wrong, their kinds, and what they used to worship","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : et leurs épouses (païennes).","explicationUnanime":"On dira aux anges ce jour-là: Rassemblez les polythéistes, qui se montraient injustes en mécroyant, avec leurs semblables et leurs partisans qui traitaient de menteurs les messagers et adoraient des idoles*en dehors d’Allah, puis montrez-leur le chemin du feu et conduisez-les à leur sort.","explicationEn":"23. On that day, it will be said to the angels, “Gather the idolaters and their like, who wronged due to their ascribing partners with Allah; all those who followed them in rejection, and all the idols they used to worship instead of Allah. And show them all the path to the hellfire; lead them on to it and drive them towards it, because it is their abode.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ فَاهْدُوهُمْ إِلَىٰ صِرَاطِ الْجَحِيمِ","tradPropre":"en dehors d'Allah. Puis conduisez-les au chemin de la Fournaise.","tradEn":"Other than Allāh, and guide them to the path of Hellfire","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On dira aux anges ce jour-là: Rassemblez les polythéistes, qui se montraient injustes en mécroyant, avec leurs semblables et leurs partisans qui traitaient de menteurs les messagers et adoraient des idoles*en dehors d’Allah, puis montrez-leur le chemin du feu et conduisez-les à leur sort.","explicationEn":"23. On that day, it will be said to the angels, “Gather the idolaters and their like, who wronged due to their ascribing partners with Allah; all those who followed them in rejection, and all the idols they used to worship instead of Allah. And show them all the path to the hellfire; lead them on to it and drive them towards it, because it is their abode.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"وَقِفُوهُمْ  إِنَّهُمْ مَسْئُولُونَ","tradPropre":"Et arrêtez-les: car ils doivent être interrogés».","tradEn":"And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Arrêtez-les avant de les faire entrer dans le feu afin qu’ils rendent des comptes, puis continuez après cela à les conduire au feu.","explicationEn":"24. “And hold them back for a while before entering them into the hellfire for them to give account, because they are to be questioned. Then after that, drive them towards the hellfire.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"مَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُونَ","tradPropre":"«Pourquoi ne vous portez-vous pas secours mutuellement?»","tradEn":"[They will be asked], \"What is [wrong] with you? Why do you not help each other?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On les admonestera en leur disant: Pour quelle raison ne portez-vous pas secours les uns aux autres à l’image de ce que vous faisiez dans le bas monde, lorsque vous prétendiez que c’était vos idoles qui vous secourraient?","explicationEn":"25. And it will be said to them in rebuke, “What is the matter with you that you are not helping each other like you used to in the world, and you used to claim that your idols would help you?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"بَلْ هُمُ الْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُونَ","tradPropre":"Mais ce jour-là, ils seront complètement soumis,","tradEn":"But they, that Day, are in surrender.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce jour-là, ils seront plutôt humblement soumis à ce qu’Allah fera d’eux et personne parmi eux ne secourra l'autre, puisqu’ils seront faibles et impuissants.","explicationEn":"26. Rather, today they are submissive to the command of Allah and humiliated, they will not help each other because of their incapability to do so, and because of their lack of strategies.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"وَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَسَاءَلُونَ","tradPropre":"et les uns se tourneront vers les autres s'interrogeant mutuellement;","tradEn":"And they will approach one another asking [i.e., blaming] each other.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils se couvriront les uns les autres de reproches et se disputeront lorsque les reproches et les disputes ne seront d’aucun secours.","explicationEn":"27. And they will turn to each other blaming each other and arguing, when shifting the blame and arguing will be of no use.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا إِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَأْتُونَنَا عَنِ الْيَمِينِ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: «C'est vous qui nous forciez (à la mécréance)».","tradEn":"They will say, \"Indeed, you used to come at us from the right.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les suiveurs diront aux meneurs: Ô nos chefs, vous prétendiez nous prêcher la religion et nous présenter la vérité lorsque vous nous embellissiez la mécréance, le polythéisme et les péchés et vous nous faisiez détester la vérité que les messagers apportaient de la part d’Allah","explicationEn":"28. The followers will say to the leaders, “O our seniors! You use to approach us in matters of religion and truth, and would beautify for us disbelief, ascribing partners with Allah and sins, while scaring us away from the truth that the messengers brought from Allah.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا بَلْ لَمْ تَكُونُوا مُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"«C'est vous plutôt (diront les chefs) qui ne vouliez pas croire.","tradEn":"They [i.e., the oppressors] will say, \"Rather, you [yourselves] were not believers,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les meneurs répondront aux suiveurs: Les choses ne sont pas telles que vous le prétendez. Vous étiez plutôt mécréants et n’étiez pas croyants. Pire, vous refusiez même la vérité.","explicationEn":"29. The leaders will say to the followers: “The matter is not as you claim it is. Rather, you yourselves were upon disbelief and were not believers; you were the rejectors.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"وَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ سُلْطَانٍ  بَلْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا طَاغِينَ","tradPropre":"Et nous n'avions aucun pouvoir sur vous. C'est vous plutôt qui étiez des gens transgresseurs.","tradEn":"And we had over you no authority, but you were a transgressing people.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô suiveurs, nous n’avions aucun pouvoir ni aucune autorité sur vous afin de vous forcer à tomber dans la mécréance, le polythéisme et les péchés. Vous étiez plutôt des gens qui dépassaient les limites de la mécréance et de l’égarement.","explicationEn":"30. “O followers! We had no power or authority over you such that we cause you to disbelieve, ascribe partners with Allah or commit sins. Rather, you were people who transgressed the limit in disbelief and deviance yourselves; we were not the ones who led you astray.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"فَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَا  إِنَّا لَذَائِقُونَ","tradPropre":"La parole de notre Seigneur s'est donc réalisée contre nous; certes, nous allons goûter [au châtiment].","tradEn":"So the word [i.e., decree] of our Lord has come into effect upon us; indeed, we will taste [punishment].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est pourquoi la menace d’Allah qui vous était adressée et nous était adressée, celle de « remplir l’Enfer de toi et de tous ceux qui t’ont suivi » (Sourate Şâd, verset 85), doit être exécutée. Ainsi, nous goûterons inexorablement à ce dont notre Seigneur nous a menacés.","explicationEn":"31. “So the promise of Allah is now imposing on us and on you, when He said, “I will surely fill Hell with you and those of them that follow you all together.” (Ṣād: 85), and because of that we are inevitably going to taste whatever our Lord has promised.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"فَأَغْوَيْنَاكُمْ إِنَّا كُنَّا غَاوِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous vous avons induits en erreur car, en vérité, nous étions égarés nous-mêmes».","tradEn":"And we led you to deviation; indeed, we were deviators.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous vous avons appelés à l’égarement et à la mécréance et nous étions vraiment égarés du chemin de la guidée.","explicationEn":"32. “So we called you towards deviance and disbelief; we had deviated from the path of guidance, but all you did was that you followed us because of your disposition to incline towards disbelief and deviance.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"فَإِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِي الْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce jour-là donc, ils seront tous associés dans le châtiment.","tradEn":"So indeed they, that Day, will be sharing in the punishment.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les suiveurs et les meneurs subiront alors le même châtiment le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"33. So the followers and the leaders will share in the punishment on the Day of Judgement; none will benefit the other in any way because they were all partners in deviance and disbelief in the world.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا كَذَالِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Ainsi traitons-Nous les criminels.","tradEn":"Indeed, that is how We deal with the criminals.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tout comme Nous faisons goûter le châtiment à ces gens, Nous le ferons goûter à d’autres criminels.","explicationEn":"34. Indeed, just as I did with these people by making them taste the punishment, I will do the same with other criminals by joining the followers and leaders in the punishment, each in proportion to whatever they deserve of it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا إِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Quand on leur disait: «Point de divinité à part Allah», ils se gonflaient d'orgueil,","tradEn":"Indeed they, when it was said to them, \"There is no deity but Allāh,\" were arrogant","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque, dans le bas monde, on disait à ces polythéistes « Il n’existe pas de divinité en dehors d’Allah » afin qu’ils œuvrent selon ce que cette formule implique et délaissent ce qui s’oppose à elle, ils refusaient de l’accepter faisant preuve d’orgueil et d’arrogance face à la vérité.","explicationEn":"35. Indeed, these idolaters, when it would be said to them in the world, “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah” so that they could act upon its requirements and leave everything that contradicted it, they would reject answering the call to it and submitting to it out of arrogance from the truth and showing haughtiness to it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"وَيَقُولُونَ أَئِنَّا لَتَارِكُو آلِهَتِنَا لِشَاعِرٍ مَجْنُونٍ","tradPropre":"et disaient: «Allons-nous abandonner nos divinités pour un poète fou?»","tradEn":"And were saying, \"Are we to leave our gods for a mad poet?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils disaient afin de justifier leur mécréance: Délaisserons-nous l’adoration de nos divinités pour les paroles d’un poète fou? C’est le Prophète qui était visé par ces paroles.","explicationEn":"36. And they would say, justifying their disbelief: “Should we leave the worship of our idols because of the words of a mad poet?” intending through this statement of theirs: the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"بَلْ جَاءَ بِالْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Il est plutôt venu avec la Vérité et il a confirmé les messagers (précédents).","tradEn":"Rather, he [i.e., the Prophet (ﷺ)] has come with the truth and confirmed the [previous] messengers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Leur accusation était immonde car le Messager d’Allah n’était ni fou ni un poète. Il a plutôt apporté le Coran qui appelle à proclamer l’Unicité d’Allah et à suivre Son Messager. Les messagers ont certainement été véridiques lorsque, par ordre d’Allah, ils ont prêché Son Unicité et ont affirmé la réalité de la Ressuscitation. Le Messager Muħammad ne les a contredits sur aucun point.","explicationEn":"37. Verily, they have spoken a grave lie, because the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was not a madman nor a poet; he brought the Qur’ān which calls towards the oneness of Allah and towards following His Messenger. He corroborated the message of monotheism and affirmation of the afterlife the messengers brought from Allah; he did not contradict them in anything.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"إِنَّكُمْ لَذَائِقُو الْعَذَابِ الْأَلِيمِ","tradPropre":"Vous allez certes, goûter au châtiment douloureux.","tradEn":"Indeed, you [disbelievers] will be tasters of the painful punishment,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô polythéistes, vous allez certainement goûter au châtiment douloureux le Jour de la Résurrection pour avoir été mécréants et pour avoir traité de menteurs les messagers.","explicationEn":"38. O idolaters! You are surely going to suffer the painful punishment on the Day of Judgement due to your disbelief and rejection of the messengers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"وَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ إِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et vous ne serez rétribués que selon ce que vous œuvriez,","tradEn":"And you will not be recompensed except for what you used to do -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô polythéistes, vous ne serez rétribués que pour votre mécréance et vos péchés commis dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"39. O idolaters! Your requital will only be for the disbelief and sins you used to commit in the world.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"sauf les serviteurs élus d'Allah,","tradEn":"But not the chosen servants of Allāh.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quant aux serviteurs croyants d’Allah, qu’Allah a choisis pour être Ses adorateurs exclusifs et qui L’adorent avec sincérité, ils échapperont à ce châtiment.","explicationEn":"40. However, the believing servants of Allah whom Allah chose for His worship, and they sincerely devoted worship to Him, will be in a place of safety from this punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"أُولَائِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌ مَعْلُومٌ","tradPropre":"Ceux-là auront une rétribution bien connue:","tradEn":"Those will have a provision determined -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces serviteurs sincères auront droit à une rétribution de la part d'Allah, connue pour être agréable et durable.","explicationEn":"41. For those sincere servants will be a special provision granted to them by Allah, well-known for its purity, beauty and eternity.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"فَوَاكِهُ  وَهُمْ مُكْرَمُونَ","tradPropre":"des fruits, et ils seront honorés,","tradEn":"Fruits; and they will be honored","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils seront, entre autres, pourvus des fruits les plus agréables qu’ils puissent goûter et désirer, en plus d’être honorés par l’élévation de leurs degrés et la vision du noble visage d’Allah.","explicationEn":"42. From this special provision will be that they are provided with the purest of fruits they ever eat and desire; on top of that they will be honoured with their ranks being raised and being able to see the blessed face of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"فِي جَنَّاتِ النَّعِيمِ","tradPropre":"dans les Jardins du délice,","tradEn":"In gardens of pleasure","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils obtiendront tout cela dans les jardins des délices éternels qui ne s’interrompent jamais ni ne disparaissent.","explicationEn":"43. All that they will get in the permanent gardens of everlasting bliss, which will never expire or cease to exist.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍ مُتَقَابِلِينَ","tradPropre":"sur des lits, face à face.","tradEn":"On thrones facing one another.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils s’accouderont sur des lits et se feront face les uns aux autres.","explicationEn":"44. They will lean on thrones opposite to and facing one another; each one happy to meet his brother.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"يُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِكَأْسٍ مِنْ مَعِينٍ","tradPropre":"On fera circuler entre eux une coupe d'eau remplie à une source","tradEn":"There will be circulated among them a cup [of wine] from a flowing spring,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On fera circuler parmi eux des coupes de vin aussi pur que de l’eau de source.","explicationEn":"45. Glasses of wine, clear like flowing water, shall be passed around them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"بَيْضَاءَ لَذَّةٍ لِلشَّارِبِينَ","tradPropre":"blanche, savoureuse à boire,","tradEn":"White and delicious to the drinkers;","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"De l’eau blanche, savoureuse à boire.","explicationEn":"46. White in colour, whoever drinks from it will enjoy a complete sensation.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"لَا فِيهَا غَوْلٌ وَلَا هُمْ عَنْهَا يُنْزَفُونَ","tradPropre":"Elle n'offusquera point leur raison et ne les enivrera pas.","tradEn":"No bad effect is there in it, nor from it will they be intoxicated.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce vin n’est pas semblable au vin du bas monde puisqu’il n’est pas enivrant et n'altère pas les facultés physiques et mentales de celui qui le boit.","explicationEn":"47. It will not be like the wine of the world; there will be no intoxication that clouds the minds, nor will it give its drinkers headaches. The bodies and minds of its drinkers will remain safe.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"وَعِنْدَهُمْ قَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرْفِ عِينٌ","tradPropre":"Et Ils auront auprès d'eux des belles aux grands yeux, au regard chaste,","tradEn":"And with them will be women limiting [their] glances, with large, [beautiful] eyes,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils auront pour compagnes au Paradis des femmes chastes qui ne regardent personne d'autre que leurs époux et ont de beaux yeux.","explicationEn":"48. In Paradise, they will also have chaste wives with beautiful eyes, who will not longingly look towards anyone other than their husbands.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"كَأَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌ مَكْنُونٌ","tradPropre":"semblables au blanc bien préservé de l'œuf.","tradEn":"As if they were [delicate] eggs, well-protected.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Leur blancheur teintée de jaune les rend semblables à l'oeuf précieux d'un oiseau, que les mains ne peuvent toucher.","explicationEn":"49. In their white complexation blended with a tinge of redness, it will be as if they were ostrich eggs covered by feathers from the wind and dust; protected and untouched by any hand.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"فَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَسَاءَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Puis les uns se tourneront vers les autres s'interrogeant mutuellement.","tradEn":"And they will approach one another, inquiring of each other.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les gens du Paradis s'adresseront les uns aux autres afin de se questionner sur leur passé et de ce qui leur est arrivé dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"50. The people of Paradise will turn to one another asking about their past, and what happened to them in the world.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"قَالَ قَائِلٌ مِنْهُمْ إِنِّي كَانَ لِي قَرِينٌ","tradPropre":"L'un d'eux dira: «J'avais un compagnon","tradEn":"A speaker among them will say, \"Indeed, I had a companion [on earth].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Un de ces croyants dira: J'avais dans le bas monde un compagnon qui niait la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"51. One of the believers will say, “Indeed, I had a companion in the world who would deny the resurrection.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"يَقُولُ أَإِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُصَدِّقِينَ","tradPropre":"qui disait: «Es-tu vraiment de ceux qui croient?","tradEn":"Who would say, 'Are you indeed of those who believe","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il me disait d’un ton railleur et moqueur: Ô mon ami, crois-tu à la résurrection des morts?","explicationEn":"52. He would say to me in denial and mockingly, “O my friend! Are you one of those who believe in the resurrection of the dead?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"أَإِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَعِظَامًا أَإِنَّا لَمَدِينُونَ","tradPropre":"Est-ce que quand nous mourrons et serons poussière et ossements, nous aurons à rendre des comptes?»","tradEn":"That when we have died and become dust and bones, we will indeed be recompensed?'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque nous mourrons et que nous deviendrons poussière et ossements, serons-nous alors ressuscités et rétribués pour les œuvres que nous avons accomplies dans le bas monde?","explicationEn":"53. “When we die and turn into dust and decayed bones, will we then be resurrected and requited for our deeds we did in the world?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"قَالَ هَلْ أَنْتُمْ مُطَّلِعُونَ","tradPropre":"Il dira: «Est-ce que vous voudriez regarder d'en haut?»","tradEn":"He will say, \"Would you [care to] look?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> A l’adresse de ses compagnons du Paradis.","explicationUnanime":"Le compagnon croyant dira à ses semblables parmi les gens du Paradis: Voyons quel est le sort de ce compagnon qui niait la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"54. His believing companion will say to his companions of the people of Paradise: “Take a look with me; let us see the outcome of that companion of mine who used to deny the resurrection.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"فَاطَّلَعَ فَرَآهُ فِي سَوَاءِ الْجَحِيمِ","tradPropre":"Alors il regardera d'en haut et il le verra en plein dans la Fournaise,","tradEn":"And he will look and see him in the midst of the Hellfire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il regardera et verra alors son ancien compagnon au milieu de l'Enfer.","explicationEn":"55. So he will take a look and see his companion in the middle of hell.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"قَالَ تَاللَّهِ إِنْ كِدْتَ لَتُرْدِينِ","tradPropre":"et dira: «Par Allah! Tu as bien failli causer ma perte!","tradEn":"He will say, \"By Allāh, you almost ruined me.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le croyant lui dira: Par Allah, tu as failli, en m’appelant à mécroire et à nier la Ressuscitation, me mener à ma perte, ô compagnon, et me faire entrer en Enfer.","explicationEn":"56. He will say: “O my companion! By Allah, you were close to dooming me to the hellfire by calling me towards disbelief and denying the resurrection!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"وَلَوْلَا نِعْمَةُ رَبِّي لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِينَ","tradPropre":"et sans le bienfait de mon Seigneur, j'aurais certainement été du nombre de ceux qu'on traîne [au supplice].","tradEn":"If not for the favor of my Lord, I would have been of those brought in [to Hell].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Selon nombre d’exégètes, ici prennent fin les reproches adressés à son ancien compagnon par le croyant. Puis ce dernier s’adresse à ses frères au Paradis (versets 58 à 60) auxquels il rappelle les grâces d’Allah. Selon d’autres, néanmoins, les versets 58 et 59 sont la suite des reproches adressés à l’impie par son ancien compagnon.","explicationUnanime":"N'était-ce le bienfait que me fit Allah en me guidant à la foi et en me la facilitant, j'aurais été du nombre de ceux qui, comme toi, ont été traînés vers leur supplice","explicationEn":"57. “Had it not been for Allah blessing me with guidance to faith and the ability to accept it, I would have been one of those brought to the punishment like you.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"أَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِينَ","tradPropre":"N'est-il pas vrai que nous ne mourrons","tradEn":"Then, are we not to die","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous autres gens du Paradis, nous ne mourrons pas.","explicationEn":"58. “We, the people of Paradise, will never die.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا مَوْتَتَنَا الْأُولَىٰ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِينَ","tradPropre":"que de notre première mort et que nous ne serons pas châtiés?»","tradEn":"Except for our first death, and we will not be punished?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La seule mort que nous connaissons est celle qui nous a fait quitter le bas monde. Au Paradis, nous vivrons éternellement et nous ne serons pas châtiés comme les mécréants.","explicationEn":"59. “Except the first death of ours in the world. Instead, we will live forever in Paradise and will not be punished like the disbelievers will be.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ هَاذَا لَهُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ","tradPropre":"C'est cela, certes, le grand succès.","tradEn":"Indeed, this is the great attainment.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Entrer au Paradis, y demeurer éternellement et échapper à l'Enfer sont des rétributions de notre Seigneur, qui représentent le succès suprême égalé par aucun autre succès.","explicationEn":"60. “Indeed, this requital of ours which our Lord has given us, i.e entry into Paradise, living in it forever and salvation from the hellfire, is the greatest, unparallelled success.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"لِمِثْلِ هَاذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ الْعَامِلُونَ","tradPropre":"C'est pour une chose pareille que doivent ouvrer ceux qui ouvrent.","tradEn":"For the like of this let the workers [on earth] work.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C'est pour mériter une telle rétribution que doivent œuvrer les gens, car ils accompliront à coup sûr une transaction gagnante.","explicationEn":"61. It is for requital like this the workers should strive for, because this is the profitable trade.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"أَذَالِكَ خَيْرٌ نُزُلًا أَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّومِ","tradPropre":"Est-ce que ceci est meilleur comme séjour, ou l'arbre de Zaqqûm?","tradEn":"Is that [i.e., Paradise] a better accommodation or the tree of zaqqūm?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les délices mentionnés, qu'Allah réserve à Ses serviteurs qui Lui obéissent sincèrement, sont-ils meilleurs et plus honorables ou bien l'arbre Az-Zaqqûm maudit dans le Coran et servant de nourriture aux mécréants, qui ne fait ni grossir ni ne calme la faim?","explicationEn":"62. Is that aforementioned bounty which Allah has prepared for His servants whom He chose to obey Him, better and more virtuous in rank and honour, than the tree of Zaqqūm which has been cursed in the Qur’ān? It is the food of the disbelievers, which neither nourishes nor satisfies hunger.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا جَعَلْنَاهَا فِتْنَةً لِلظَّالِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous l'avons assigné en épreuve aux injustes.","tradEn":"Indeed, We have made it a torment for the wrongdoers.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Qui s’étonnèrent qu’un arbre puisse pousser en Enfer sans savoir que les réalités de l’au-delà ne sont en rien comparables à celles d’ici-bas.","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons fait de cet arbre un trouble pour ceux qui commettent l'injustice de la mécréance et des péchés, puisqu'ils disent: Le feu consume les arbres et c'est pour cette raison que cet arbre ne peut pousser en Enfer.","explicationEn":"63. I have made this tree a trial, with which those who do wrong through disbelief and sins are tested, when they say: “Indeed, fire consumes trees, so it is impossible that it grows in the hellfire.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِي أَصْلِ الْجَحِيمِ","tradPropre":"C'est un arbre qui sort du fond de la Fournaise.","tradEn":"Indeed, it is a tree issuing from the bottom of the Hellfire,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L'arbre Az-Zaqqûm est un arbre détestable qui pousse au fond de l'Enfer.","explicationEn":"64. Indeed, the tree of Zaqqūm is a disgusting tree, and is one that comes out of the depth of hell.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"طَلْعُهَا كَأَنَّهُ رُءُوسُ الشَّيَاطِينِ","tradPropre":"Ses fruits sont comme des têtes de diables.","tradEn":"Its emerging fruit as if it was heads of the devils.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ses fruits sont hideux et ressemblent à des têtes de démons. Or cette apparence hideuse indique que le goût est abominable.","explicationEn":"65. The fruits that come out of it are ugly in appearance, like the heads of satans. The ugliness in appearance is a sign of ugliness in nature, which means they revolting in taste.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"فَإِنَّهُمْ لَآكِلُونَ مِنْهَا فَمَالِئُونَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils doivent certainement en manger et ils doivent s'en remplir le ventre.","tradEn":"And indeed, they will eat from it and fill with it their bellies.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les mécréants mangeront de ces fruits amers et écœurants et en empliront leurs ventres vides.","explicationEn":"66. Indeed, the disbelievers will eat from its bitter, ugly fruits, and fill their empty bellies with them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ إِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًا مِنْ حَمِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Ensuite ils auront par-dessus une mixture d'eau bouillante.","tradEn":"Then indeed, they will have after it a mixture of scalding water.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis après avoir mangé cette nourriture, ils ingurgiteront une boisson faite d'un mélange de liquides nauséabonds et bouillants.","explicationEn":"67. Then, after having eaten them, they will have a disgusting, boiling cocktail to drink.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ إِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَإِلَى الْجَحِيمِ","tradPropre":"Puis leur retour sera vers la Fournaise.","tradEn":"Then indeed, their return will be to the Hellfire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils retourneront ensuite à leur châtiment en Enfer afin de subir des supplices successifs.","explicationEn":"68. Then, their return after that will be to the punishment of hell; they will move from one punishment to another.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُمْ أَلْفَوْا آبَاءَهُمْ ضَالِّينَ","tradPropre":"C'est qu'ils ont trouvé leurs ancêtres dans l'égarement,","tradEn":"Indeed they found their fathers astray.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces mécréants ont trouvé leurs ancêtres dans l'égarement et les ont donc suivis par imitation et non sur la base de preuves.","explicationEn":"69. Indeed, these disbelievers found their forefathers astray from the path of guidance and followed them blindly without proof of their truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"فَهُمْ عَلَىٰ آثَارِهِمْ يُهْرَعُونَ","tradPropre":"et les voilà courant sur leurs traces.","tradEn":"So they hastened [to follow] in their footsteps.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils s'empressent donc de les suivre dans l'égarement.","explicationEn":"70. So they hastily followed the footsteps of their forefathers in deviance, as if they were harassed and forced into doing so.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ أَكْثَرُ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"En effet, avant eux, la plupart des anciens se sont égarés.","tradEn":"And there had already strayed before them most of the former peoples,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Bien avant eux, de nombreux anciens se sont égarés. Ton peuple n'est donc pas le premier à s'être égaré, ô Messager.","explicationEn":"71. Verily, the majority of people before them also went astray. So O Messenger, those to whom you have been sent are not the first to go astray.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا فِيهِمْ مُنْذِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous avions certes envoyé parmi eux des avertisseurs.","tradEn":"And We had already sent among them warners.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons envoyé à ces anciens peuples des Messagers qui les menaçaient du châtiment d'Allah mais ils préfèrent mécroire.","explicationEn":"72. Verily, I sent to the previous nations messengers who would warn them of the punishment of Allah, but they disbelieved.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Regarde donc ce qu'il est advenu de ceux qui ont été avertis!","tradEn":"Then look how was the end of those who were warned -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Regarde, ô Messager, quelle fut la fin des peuples qui n'ont pas tenu compte des avertissements de leurs messagers. Leur fin fut d'entrer en Enfer et d'y demeurer éternellement pour avoir été mécréants et pour avoir traité de menteurs leurs messagers.","explicationEn":"73. O Messenger! See what the outcome was of the nations who were warned by their messengers but did not accept their warning! Indeed, their outcome was entering into the hellfire having to live in it forever due to their disbelief and rejection of their messengers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"Exception faite des élus, parmi les serviteurs d'Allah:","tradEn":"But not the chosen servants of Allāh.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il sera fait exception de ceux qu'Allah a élus afin qu’ils croient en Lui. Ils seront sauvés du châtiment décrété comme destination finale de ces dénégateurs mécréants.","explicationEn":"74. Except for those whom Allah chose to believe in Him and His oneness; they were saved from the punishment which was the outcome of the disbelieving rejectors.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ نَادَانَا نُوحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ الْمُجِيبُونَ","tradPropre":"Noé, en effet, fit appel à Nous qui sommes le Meilleur Répondeur (qui exauce les prières).","tradEn":"And Noah had certainly called Us, and [We are] the best of responders.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Notre prophète Noé Nous a invoqué contre son peuple qui l'a traité de menteur et Nous étions le Meilleur Répondeur, puisque Nous l'avons rapidement exaucé.","explicationEn":"75. Verily, My Prophet Noah (peace be upon him) called out to Me when he supplicated against his people who had rejected him. I am the best of answerers; I quickly answered his supplication against his people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"وَنَجَّيْنَاهُ وَأَهْلَهُ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيمِ","tradPropre":"Et Nous le sauvâmes, lui et sa famille, de la grande angoisse,","tradEn":"And We saved him and his family from the great affliction.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Débute donc ici le récit détaillé de ces peuples mentionnés peu avant et qui furent anéantis pour avoir renié leurs Messagers.","explicationUnanime":"Nous l'avons sauvé lui, sa famille et les croyants qui l'accompagnaient des persécutions de son peuple et de la noyade dans le Grand Déluge envoyé contre les mécréants de ce peuple.","explicationEn":"76. And I saved him, together with members of his household and the believers with him from the harm of his people and from drowning in the great flood, which was sent upon the disbelievers from his people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهُ هُمُ الْبَاقِينَ","tradPropre":"et Nous fîmes de sa descendance les seuls survivants.","tradEn":"And We made his descendants those remaining [on the earth]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons sauvé sa famille et ses disciples croyants seuls. Quant aux mécréants restants de son peuple, Nous les avons anéantis.","explicationEn":"77. I saved his family members and his believing followers only, because I drowned the others from his disbelieving nation.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِي الْآخِرِينَ","tradPropre":"et Nous avons perpétué son souvenir dans la postérité,","tradEn":"And left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons fait en sorte que les peuples futurs le mentionnent en bien.","explicationEn":"78. And I left a good legacy for him in the nations that would come after, who would praise Noah and always mention him with good.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ نُوحٍ فِي الْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"Paix sur Noé dans tout l'univers!","tradEn":"\"Peace upon Noah among the worlds.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que la sécurité et la paix soient avec Noé. On ne dira aucun mal de lui dans les générations futures. On ferra plutôt son éloge et on le mentionnera en bien.","explicationEn":"79. It is a security and safety for Noah from the following nations saying evil regarding him. Instead, praise and positive mention of him will remain.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا كَذَالِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Ainsi récompensons-Nous les bienfaisants.","tradEn":"Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cette rétribution que Nous avons accordée à Noé est celle réservée à ceux qui excellent dans leur adoration et obéissent à Allah Seul.","explicationEn":"80. Indeed, I grant those who do good through their worship and obedience to Me alone, the same type of reward I granted to Noah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Il était, certes, un de Nos serviteurs croyants.","tradEn":"Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Noé était du nombre de Nos serviteurs croyants qui obéissaient à Allah.","explicationEn":"81. Noah was definitely one of My servants who believed and acted according to My obedience.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا الْآخَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite Nous noyâmes les autres.","tradEn":"Then We drowned the others [i.e., disbelievers].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous noyâmes ceux qui restèrent dans le Déluge que Nous avons envoyé sur eux et aucun d'eux n'en réchappa.","explicationEn":"82. Then, I drowned the rest by the flood I sent upon them. None of them remained.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"۞ وَإِنَّ مِنْ شِيعَتِهِ لَإِبْرَاهِيمَ","tradPropre":"Du nombre de ses coreligionnaires, certes, fut Abraham.","tradEn":"And indeed, among his kind was Abraham,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Abraham était du nombre des coreligionnaires de Noé, qui ont appelé, comme lui, à proclamer l'Unicité d'Allah.","explicationEn":"83. Indeed, Abraham was someone on the same religion as Noah, and he also called to the Oneness of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"إِذْ جَاءَ رَبَّهُ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Quand il vint à son Seigneur avec un cœur sain.","tradEn":"When he came to his Lord with a sound heart","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Rappelle-toi lorsqu'il vint à son Seigneur avec un cœur exempt de polythéisme et empli du désir de conseiller les gens sur l'adoration d’Allah.","explicationEn":"84. Remember when he came to his Lord with a heart pure from ascribing partners to Allah and from doubts, full of sincerity to Allah only wanted good for the creation.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوْمِهِ مَاذَا تَعْبُدُونَ","tradPropre":"Quand il dit à son père et à son peuple: «Qu'est-ce que vous adorez?»","tradEn":"[And] when he said to his father and his people, \"What do you worship?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu'il dit à son père et à son peuple polythéiste sur un ton réprobateur: Qu'adorez-vous donc en dehors d'Allah?","explicationEn":"85. When he said to his father and his idolatrous nation, rebuking them, “What do you worship instead of Allah?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"أَئِفْكًا آلِهَةً دُونَ اللَّهِ تُرِيدُونَ","tradPropre":"Cherchez-vous dans votre égarement, des divinités en dehors d'Allah?","tradEn":"Is it falsehood [as] gods other than Allāh you desire?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces divinités inventées que vous adorez en dehors de Lui?","explicationEn":"86. “O my people, do you prefer to worship idols besides Allah basing your worship on a completely fabricated lie?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"فَمَا ظَنُّكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"Que pensez-vous du Seigneur des mondes?»","tradEn":"Then what is your thought about the Lord of the worlds?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : quelle est donc cette opinion (erronée) que vous vous faites du Seigneur de la Création ?","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, que pensez-vous qu'Allah fera de vous lorsque vous Le rencontrerez alors que vous adoriez des idoles en dehors de Lui?","explicationEn":"87. “O my people! What do you think will happen when you meet the Lord of the worlds, while you used to worship things other than Him? What do you think He will do to you?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"فَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةً فِي النُّجُومِ","tradPropre":"Puis, il jeta un regard attentif sur les étoiles,","tradEn":"And he cast a look at the stars","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Réfléchissant au prétexte qu’il pourrait inventer pour ne pas participer à la fête païenne que son peuple s’apprête à célébrer, expliquent nombre d’exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Abraham regarda les étoiles afin de mettre au point un stratagème lui épargnant de sortir avec les siens.","explicationEn":"88. So Abraham took a glance at the stars, hatching a plan to come out of having to go out with his people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-89.html"},{"numVerset":89,"texteArabe":"فَقَالَ إِنِّي سَقِيمٌ","tradPropre":"et dit: «Je suis malade».","tradEn":"And said, \"Indeed, I am [about to be] ill.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ces mots ne sont pas en soi mensongers puisqu’il était bel et bien « malade » de leurs pratiques idolâtres.","explicationUnanime":"Afin de ne pas se rendre avec eux sur leur lieu de festivité, il leur dit en guise d'excuse: Je suis malade.","explicationEn":"89. He said, presenting an excuse from having to go with his people to their festival, “I am sick.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037089","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-88.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-90.html"},{"numVerset":90,"texteArabe":"فَتَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils lui tournèrent le dos et s'en allèrent.","tradEn":"So they turned away from him, departing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils le laissèrent alors derrière eux et s'en allèrent.","explicationEn":"90. So they left him behind and went.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037090","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-89.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-91.html"},{"numVerset":91,"texteArabe":"فَرَاغَ إِلَىٰ آلِهَتِهِمْ فَقَالَ أَلَا تَأْكُلُونَ","tradPropre":"Alors il se glissa vers leurs divinités et dit: «Ne mangez-vous pas?","tradEn":"Then he turned to their gods and said, \"Do you not eat?","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Cette nourriture qui vous est présentée en offrande par vos adorateurs.","explicationUnanime":"Il se rendit auprès des divinités qu'ils adoraient en dehors d'Allah et leur dit d’un ton railleur: Ne mangez-vous pas la nourriture que les polythéistes vous offrent?","explicationEn":"91. He turned towards the idols they would worship instead of Allah, and said mocking them, “Will you not eat from the food the idolaters make for you?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037091","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-90.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-92.html"},{"numVerset":92,"texteArabe":"مَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنْطِقُونَ","tradPropre":"Qu'avez-vous à ne pas parler?»","tradEn":"What is [wrong] with you that you do not speak?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pourquoi ne parlez-vous pas, ni ne répondez à celui qui vous interroge? Est-ce de telles divinités que l'on adore en dehors d'Allah?","explicationEn":"92. “What is the matter with you that you do not speak, nor answer whoever asks you? Can this type of thing be worshipped instead of Allah?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037092","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-91.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-93.html"},{"numVerset":93,"texteArabe":"فَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًا بِالْيَمِينِ","tradPropre":"Puis il se mit furtivement à les frapper de sa main droite.","tradEn":"And he turned upon them a blow with [his] right hand.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il se mit ensuite à les frapper de sa main droite dans la finalité de les briser.","explicationEn":"93. Then, Abraham started hitting them with his right hand, intending to break them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037093","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-92.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-94.html"},{"numVerset":94,"texteArabe":"فَأَقْبَلُوا إِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّونَ","tradPropre":"Alors [les gens] vinrent à lui en courant.","tradEn":"Then they [i.e., the people] came toward him, hastening.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les adorateurs de ces divinités revinrent précipitamment.","explicationEn":"94. So the worshippers of these idols came rushing to him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037094","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-93.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-95.html"},{"numVerset":95,"texteArabe":"قَالَ أَتَعْبُدُونَ مَا تَنْحِتُونَ","tradPropre":"Il [leur] dit: «Adorez-vous ce que vous-mêmes sculptez,","tradEn":"He said, \"Do you worship that which you [yourselves] carve,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Abraham leur fit face avec aplomb et les admonesta en ces termes: Adorez-vous en dehors d'Allah, des divinités que vous façonnez de vos mains?","explicationEn":"95. But Abraham countered them with steadfastness, and said to them rebuking them, “Do you worship idols instead of Allah, which you carve with your own hands?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037095","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-94.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-96.html"},{"numVerset":96,"texteArabe":"وَاللَّهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"alors que c'est Allah qui vous a créés, vous et ce que vous fabriquez?»","tradEn":"While Allāh created you and that which you do?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tandis qu'Allah vous a créés et a créé ce que vous fabriquez, et entre autres vos idoles? Il est Celui qui mérite d'être adoré Seul et que rien ne Lui soit associé.","explicationEn":"96. “While Allah (may He be glorified) is the one who created your bodies and your actions; the making of these idols are also from your actions, so He is most deserving that you worship Him alone and not ascribe partners with Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037096","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-95.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-97.html"},{"numVerset":97,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا ابْنُوا لَهُ بُنْيَانًا فَأَلْقُوهُ فِي الْجَحِيمِ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Qu'on lui construise un four et qu'on le lance dans la fournaise!»","tradEn":"They said, \"Construct for him a structure [i.e., furnace] and throw him into the burning fire.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu'ils furent incapables de répondre à Abraham sur le terrain de l'argumentation, ils eurent recours à la force et se concertèrent pour savoir ce qu'ils allaient faire de lui. Ils dirent: Elevez une construction, remplissez-la de bois, mettez le feu à ce bois et jetez Abraham dans la fournaise.","explicationEn":"97. When they became speechless to his clear reasoning they resorted to violence, and consulted with each other about what they should do with Abraham. They said, “Build a structure from him, fill it with firewood and set it on fire, then throw him into it.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037097","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-96.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-98.html"},{"numVerset":98,"texteArabe":"فَأَرَادُوا بِهِ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنَاهُمُ الْأَسْفَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils voulurent lui jouer un mauvais tour; mais ce sont eux que Nous mîmes à bas.","tradEn":"And they intended for him a plan [i.e., harm], but We made them the most debased.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le peuple d'Abraham voulut lui faire du mal et se débarrasser de lui, mais Nous les rendîmes perdants lorsque Nous avons changé le feu en fraîcheur salutaire.","explicationEn":"98. So the people of Abraham intended to do evil to Abraham by destroying him so they could be saved from him, but I made them the losers when I made the fire cool and safe for him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037098","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-97.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-99.html"},{"numVerset":99,"texteArabe":"وَقَالَ إِنِّي ذَاهِبٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّي سَيَهْدِينِ","tradPropre":"Et il dit: «Moi, je pars vers mon Seigneur et Il me guidera.","tradEn":"And [then] he said, \"Indeed, I will go to [where I am ordered by] my Lord; He will guide me.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Abraham dit: Je migrerai vers mon Seigneur et quitterai le pays de mon peuple afin de pouvoir L'adorer. Mon Seigneur m'orientera assurément vers ce qui est bon pour moi dans le bas monde et dans l'au-delà.","explicationEn":"99. Abraham said, “I am going to emigrate to my Lord and leave the city of my people so that I am able worship Him. My Lord will guide me to whatever is good for me in the world and the Hereafter.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037099","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-98.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-100.html"},{"numVerset":100,"texteArabe":"رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ","tradPropre":"Seigneur, fais-moi don d'une [progéniture] d'entre les vertueux».","tradEn":"My Lord, grant me [a child] from among the righteous.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Seigneur, fais-moi don d'une progéniture vertueuse qui m'assistera et me compensera pour l'absence des miens lorsque je serai en exil.","explicationEn":"100. “O my Lord! Grant me a pious child who will be a means of help for me and a substitute for me from my people in the wilderness.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037100","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-99.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-101.html"},{"numVerset":101,"texteArabe":"فَبَشَّرْنَاهُ بِغُلَامٍ حَلِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Nous lui fîmes donc la bonne annonce d'un garçon (Ismaël) longanime.","tradEn":"So We gave him good tidings of a forbearing boy.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Isaac, selon certains, ou Ismaël, selon d’autres exégètes dont l’avis s’appuie notamment sur le verset 112 de cette même sourate où Allah annonce la naissance d’Isaac.","explicationUnanime":"Nous l'exauçâmes et lui annonçâmes une nouvelle qui le réjouit. Nous lui annonçâmes en effet la naissance prochaine d'un fils qui vivra, grandira et atteindra l'âge adulte. Ce fils est Ismaël.","explicationEn":"101. So I answered his supplication for him and gave him news which pleased him, when I gave him the good news of a child who would grow old and become forbearing. This child was Ishmael (peace be upon him).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037101","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-100.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-102.html"},{"numVerset":102,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْيَ قَالَ يَا بُنَيَّ إِنِّي أَرَىٰ فِي الْمَنَامِ أَنِّي أَذْبَحُكَ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرَىٰ  قَالَ يَا أَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ  سَتَجِدُنِي إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الصَّابِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Puis quand celui-ci fut en âge de l'accompagner, [Abraham] dit: «O mon fils, je me vois en songe en train de t'immoler. Vois donc ce que tu en penses». (Ismaël) dit: «O mon cher père, fais ce qui t'es commandé: tu me trouveras, s'il plaît à Allah, du nombre des endurants».","tradEn":"And when he reached with him [the age of] exertion, he said, \"O my son, indeed I have seen in a dream that I [must] sacrifice you, so see what you think.\" He said, \"O my father, do as you are commanded. You will find me, if Allāh wills, of the steadfast.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu'Ismaël devint un jeune homme et que sa force physique devint aussi grande que celle de son père, celui-ci eut une vision, sachant que s'agissant d'un prophète, la vision est une forme de révélation. Abraham raconta à son fils cette vision en ces termes: Ô mon fils, j'ai vu en rêve que je t'égorgeais. Dis-moi ce que tu en penses. Ismaël répondit: Ô mon père, exécute l'ordre que t'a donné Allah de m'égorger. Tu me trouveras du nombre des endurants qui sont satisfaits du jugement d'Allah.","explicationEn":"102. When Ishmael grew into a youth and reached working age, his father Abraham saw a dream. The dreams of prophets are a form of divine revelation, so Abraham said to his son, informing him of the meaning of this dream, “O my son! Indeed, I saw in my sleep that I am slaughtering you; what is your opinion in the matter?” Ishmael replied to him saying, “O my father! Do whatever Allah has commanded you to do in slaughtering me. You will find me one of those who are patient and content with the order of Allah.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037102","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-101.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-103.html"},{"numVerset":103,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُ لِلْجَبِينِ","tradPropre":"Puis quand tous deux se furent soumis (à l'ordre d'Allah) et qu'il l'eut jeté sur le front,","tradEn":"And when they had both submitted and he put him down upon his forehead,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis lorsque tous deux se soumirent à Allah et se résignèrent à Son ordre, Abraham allongea son fils sur le front afin d’exécuter l'ordre d'Allah de l’immoler.","explicationEn":"103. So when they submitted to Allah and obeyed him, Abraham laid his son down on his forehead, to carry out the order given to him to slaughter his son.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037103","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-102.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-104.html"},{"numVerset":104,"texteArabe":"وَنَادَيْنَاهُ أَنْ يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ","tradPropre":"voilà que Nous l'appelâmes «Abraham!","tradEn":"We called to him, \"O Abraham,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous l’appelâmes alors, tandis qu’il était sur le point de passer à l'acte, et lui dîmes: « Ô Abraham ».","explicationEn":"104. I called out to Abraham while he was about to carry out the order of Allah to slaughter his son, saying: “O Abraham!”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037104","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-103.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-105.html"},{"numVerset":105,"texteArabe":"قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّؤْيَا  إِنَّا كَذَالِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Tu as confirmé la vision. C'est ainsi que Nous récompensons les bienfaisants».","tradEn":"You have fulfilled the vision.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> En étant déterminé à sacrifier ton fils.","explicationUnanime":"Tu as mis à exécution la vision que tu as eue en étant sur le point d’égorger ton fils. Tout comme Nous t’avons rétribué en te délivrant de cette immense épreuve, Nous rétribuons les bienfaisants en les délivrant des épreuves et des malheurs.","explicationEn":"105. “You have fulfilled the dream you saw in your sleep by resolving to slaughter your son. Just as I rewarded you by freeing you of this great trial, I also reward those who do good by saving them from trials and difficulties.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037105","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-104.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-106.html"},{"numVerset":106,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ هَاذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلَاءُ الْمُبِينُ","tradPropre":"C'était là certes, l'épreuve manifeste.","tradEn":"Indeed, this was the clear trial.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’était certainement une épreuve manifeste que subit Abraham et il la passa avec succès.","explicationEn":"106. Indeed, this was a clear test which Abraham passed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037106","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-105.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-107.html"},{"numVerset":107,"texteArabe":"وَفَدَيْنَاهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Et Nous le rançonnâmes d'une immolation généreuse.","tradEn":"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice,","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Un bélier qu’Abraham sacrifia à la place de son fils.","explicationUnanime":"Nous remplaçâmes le sacrifice d’Ismaël par celui d’un bélier imposant.","explicationEn":"107. And I set Ishmael free in exchange for a huge ram which was to be slaughtered instead of him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037107","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-106.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-108.html"},{"numVerset":108,"texteArabe":"وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِي الْآخِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous perpétuâmes son renom dans la postérité:","tradEn":"And We left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous fîmes en sorte qu’il soit fait éloge du nom d’Abraham dans les générations suivantes.","explicationEn":"108. I preserved good praise for Abraham to remain among the following nations.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037108","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-107.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-109.html"},{"numVerset":109,"texteArabe":"سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ إِبْرَاهِيمَ","tradPropre":"«Paix sur Abraham».","tradEn":"\"Peace upon Abraham.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salutation d’Allah sur Abraham et que tout mal lui soit épargné.","explicationEn":"109. As a commemoration for Abraham from Allah, and a prayer to keep him safe from every harm and difficulty.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037109","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-108.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-110.html"},{"numVerset":110,"texteArabe":"كَذَالِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Ainsi récompensons-Nous les bienfaisants;","tradEn":"Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tout comme Nous avons rétribué Abraham pour son obéissance, Nous rétribuons de la même façon les bienfaisants.","explicationEn":"110. Just as I requited Abraham with this reward for his obedience, I also reward those who do good.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037110","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-109.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-111.html"},{"numVerset":111,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"car il était de Nos serviteurs croyants.","tradEn":"Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Abraham était du nombre de Nos serviteurs croyants qui s’acquittaient des obligations imposées par le statut de serviteur d’Allah.","explicationEn":"111. Indeed, Abraham was one of My believing servants who fulfilled the demands of his servitude to Me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037111","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-110.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-112.html"},{"numVerset":112,"texteArabe":"وَبَشَّرْنَاهُ بِإِسْحَاقَ نَبِيًّا مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous lui fîmes la bonne annonce d'Isaac comme prophète d'entre les gens vertueux.","tradEn":"And We gave him good tidings of Isaac, a prophet from among the righteous.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En guise de rétribution pour son obéissance à Allah lorsqu’il fut sur le point d’immoler son seul fils Ismaël, Nous lui annonçâmes la naissance d’un autre fils qui deviendra prophète et serviteur vertueux: Isaac.","explicationEn":"112. And I gave him glad tidings of another son who would become a Prophet and a pious servant: he was Isaac. It was another reward for his obedience to Allah by resolving to slaughter his only son, Ishmael.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037112","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-111.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-113.html"},{"numVerset":113,"texteArabe":"وَبَارَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَىٰ إِسْحَاقَ  وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَظَالِمٌ لِنَفْسِهِ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"Et Nous le bénîmes ainsi que Isaac. Parmi leurs descendances il y a [l'homme] de bien et celui qui est manifestement injuste envers lui-même.","tradEn":"And We blessed him and Isaac. But among their descendants is the doer of good and the clearly unjust to himself [i.e., sinner].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons fait descendre sur lui et sur son fils Isaac une bénédiction de notre part et leur avons fait don de nombreux bienfaits, parmi lesquels une progéniture prolifique. Leur descendance était composée de gens bienfaisants et obéissants à leur Seigneur, et d’autres manifestement injustes envers eux-mêmes par leur mécréance et leurs péchés.","explicationEn":"113. And I showered upon him and his son Isaac My special blessings and gave them both many bounties, from which one was an increase in offspring. There were those in their progeny who did good by obeying their Lord, and those who clearly wronged themselves by disbelief and committing sins.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037113","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-112.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-114.html"},{"numVerset":114,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous accordâmes certes à Moïse et Aaron des faveurs,","tradEn":"And We did certainly confer favor upon Moses and Aaron.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons accordé à Moïse et à son frère Aaron la faveur de la prophétie.","explicationEn":"114. And verily I favoured Moses and his brother Aaron with messengership.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037114","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-113.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-115.html"},{"numVerset":115,"texteArabe":"وَنَجَّيْنَاهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيمِ","tradPropre":"Et les sauvâmes ainsi que leur peuple, de la grande angoisse,","tradEn":"And We saved them and their people from the great affliction,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les avons sauvés ainsi que leur peuple, les Israélites, de l’asservissement de Pharaon et de la noyade.","explicationEn":"115. I saved them and their nation, the Israelites, from Pharaoh enslaving them and from drowning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037115","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-114.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-116.html"},{"numVerset":116,"texteArabe":"وَنَصَرْنَاهُمْ فَكَانُوا هُمُ الْغَالِبِينَ","tradPropre":"et les secourûmes, et ils furent eux les vainqueurs.","tradEn":"And We supported them so it was they who overcame.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les avons secourus contre Pharaon et ses soldats et ils eurent alors le dessus sur leur ennemi.","explicationEn":"116. I also helped them against Pharaoh and his armies, so they had the upper hand over their enemies.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037116","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-115.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-117.html"},{"numVerset":117,"texteArabe":"وَآتَيْنَاهُمَا الْكِتَابَ الْمُسْتَبِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous leur apportâmes le livre explicite","tradEn":"And We gave them the explicit Scripture [i.e., the Torah],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons donné à Moïse et à son frère Aaron la Torah en guise de Livre provenant d’Allah, clair et ne contenant aucune ambigüité.","explicationEn":"117. I gave Moses and his brother Aaron the Torah; a clear book from Allah in which there was no doubt.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037117","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-116.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-118.html"},{"numVerset":118,"texteArabe":"وَهَدَيْنَاهُمَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ","tradPropre":"et les guidâmes vers le droit chemin.","tradEn":"And We guided them on the straight path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les avons guidés vers le droit chemin qui ne comporte aucune tortuosité, la religion de l’Islam qui mène à l’agrément du Créateur.","explicationEn":"118. I also guided them towards the straight path in which there was no deviance. It was the path of the religion of Islam which led to the pleasure of the Creator (may He be glorified).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037118","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-117.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-119.html"},{"numVerset":119,"texteArabe":"وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِي الْآخِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous perpétuâmes leur renom dans la postérité:","tradEn":"And We left for them [favorable mention] among later generations:","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous fîmes en sorte que leurs noms soient mentionnés avec éloge par les générations suivantes.","explicationEn":"119. And I also preserved for them positive mention and good praise among the following nations.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037119","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-118.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-120.html"},{"numVerset":120,"texteArabe":"سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ","tradPropre":"«Paix sur Moïse et Aaron»","tradEn":"\"Peace upon Moses and Aaron.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salutation agréable à Moïse et Aaron, qu’il leur soit fait éloge et que tout mal leur soit épargné.","explicationEn":"120. As a commemoration from Allah for them, in praise of them and as a prayer for safety from every harm.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037120","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-119.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-121.html"},{"numVerset":121,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا كَذَالِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Ainsi récompensons-Nous les bienfaisants;","tradEn":"Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tout comme Nous avons agréablement rétribué Moïse et Aaron, Nous rétribuons également les bienfaisants qui obéissent à leur Seigneur.","explicationEn":"121. Just as I requited Moses and Aaron with this good reward, I also reward those who do good by obeying their Lord.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037121","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-120.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-122.html"},{"numVerset":122,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"car ils étaient du nombre de Nos serviteurs croyants.","tradEn":"Indeed, they were of Our believing servants.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse et Aaron étaient du nombre de Nos serviteurs croyant, qui mettent en pratique ce qu’Allah leur a prescrit.","explicationEn":"122. Indeed, Moses and Aaron were two of My servants who believed in me and strove to do that which I legislated for them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037122","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-121.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-123.html"},{"numVerset":123,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ إِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Elie était, certes, du nombre des Messagers.","tradEn":"And indeed, Elias was from among the messengers,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Elie était du nombre de ceux qui ont été envoyés par leur Seigneur. Allah lui fit don de la prophétie et de la mission de transmettre le Message.","explicationEn":"123. Indeed, Elias was one of the messengers sent by his Lord. He blessed him with messengership and prophethood.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037123","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-122.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-124.html"},{"numVerset":124,"texteArabe":"إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ","tradPropre":"Quand il dit à son peuple: «Ne craignez-vous pas [Allah]?»","tradEn":"When he said to his people, \"Will you not fear Allāh?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il dit à son peuple, des Israélites, à qui il fut envoyé: Ô mon peuple, ne craignez-vous pas Allah en vous conformant à Ses commandements, parmi lesquels le monothéisme, et en renonçant à Ses interdits, parmi lesquels le polythéisme?","explicationEn":"124. Remember when he said to his people whom he was sent towards from the Israelites, “O my people! Will you not fear Allah by fulfilling His commands, of which is monotheism, and refraining from the things He has not allowed, from which is ascribing partners with Him?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037124","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-123.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-125.html"},{"numVerset":125,"texteArabe":"أَتَدْعُونَ بَعْلًا وَتَذَرُونَ أَحْسَنَ الْخَالِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Invoquerez-vous Ball (une idole) et délaisserez-vous le Meilleur des créateurs,","tradEn":"Do you call upon Baʿl and leave the best of creators -","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Idole à laquelle les Hébreux vouaient un culte à cette époque.","explicationUnanime":"Adorez-vous votre idole Baal et délaissez-vous l’adoration d’Allah, le Meilleur des créateurs?","explicationEn":"125. “Do you worship your idol Ba‘l instead of Allah and leave the worship of Allah who is the best of creators?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037125","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-124.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-126.html"},{"numVerset":126,"texteArabe":"اللَّهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ آبَائِكُمُ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"Allah, votre Seigneur et le Seigneur de vos plus anciens ancêtres?»","tradEn":"Allāh, your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah est votre Seigneur qui vous créa et créa vos aïeux avant vous. C’est Lui donc qui mérite d’être adoré et non vos idoles qui ne sont ni utiles ni nuisibles.","explicationEn":"126. “Allah is your lord who created you and created your forefathers before you; He is the most deserving of worship, not anything else like the idols which cannot benefit nor harm.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037126","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-125.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-127.html"},{"numVerset":127,"texteArabe":"فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَإِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils le traitèrent de menteur. Et bien, ils seront emmenées (au châtiment).","tradEn":"And they denied him, so indeed, they will be brought [for punishment],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La seule réponse de son peuple fut de le traiter de menteur et pour cette raison, ils seront châtiés.","explicationEn":"127. The only response of his nation was that they rejected him, and because of their rejection they will be brought to the punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037127","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-126.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-128.html"},{"numVerset":128,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"Exception faite des serviteurs élus d'Allah.","tradEn":"Except the chosen servants of Allāh.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il sera fait exception des croyants parmi eux, sincères dans leur adoration d’Allah. Ceux-là seront épargnés.","explicationEn":"128. Except for those who were believers and devoted their worship to Allah alone; they will be saved from being brought to the punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037128","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-127.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-129.html"},{"numVerset":129,"texteArabe":"وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِي الْآخِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous perpétuâmes son renom dans la postérité:","tradEn":"And We left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous fîmes en sorte que son nom soit mentionné avec éloge dans les générations suivantes.","explicationEn":"129. And I also preserved for him positive mention and good praise among the following nations.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037129","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-128.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-130.html"},{"numVerset":130,"texteArabe":"سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ إِلْ يَاسِينَ","tradPropre":"«Paix sur Elie et ses adeptes».","tradEn":"\"Peace upon Elias.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salutation et éloge d’Allah sur Elie.","explicationEn":"130. As a commemoration from Allah and praise for Elias.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037130","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-129.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-131.html"},{"numVerset":131,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا كَذَالِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Ainsi récompensons-Nous les bienfaisants,","tradEn":"Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tout comme Nous avons agréablement rétribué Elie, Nous rétribuons également les bienfaisants parmi Nos serviteurs croyants.","explicationEn":"131. Just as I requited Elias with this good reward, I also reward those of My believing servants who do good.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037131","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-130.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-132.html"},{"numVerset":132,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"car il était du nombre de Nos serviteurs croyants.","tradEn":"Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Elie était certainement du nombre de Nos serviteurs qui étaient sincères dans leur foi en leur Seigneur.","explicationEn":"132. Indeed, Elias was one of My true believing servants who are sincere in their belief in Me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037132","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-131.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-133.html"},{"numVerset":133,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ لُوطًا لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Loût était, certes, du nombre des Messagers.","tradEn":"And indeed, Lot was among the messengers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Loth était du nombre des messagers d’Allah chargés d’annoncer la bonne nouvelle à leur peuple et de les avertir.","explicationEn":"133. And indeed, Lot was one of the messengers of Allah who were sent to their people as bearers of good news and warners.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037133","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-132.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-134.html"},{"numVerset":134,"texteArabe":"إِذْ نَجَّيْنَاهُ وَأَهْلَهُ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"Quand Nous le sauvâmes, lui et sa famille, tout entière,","tradEn":"[So mention] when We saved him and his family, all,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Rappelle-toi lorsque Nous le sauvâmes lui et sa famille du châtiment qui s’est abattu sur son peuple.","explicationEn":"134. So remember when I saved him and members of his household from the punishment that was sent upon his people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037134","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-133.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-135.html"},{"numVerset":135,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عَجُوزًا فِي الْغَابِرِينَ","tradPropre":"sauf une vieille femme qui devait disparaître avec les autres,","tradEn":"Except an old woman [i.e., his wife] among those who remained [with the evildoers].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Seule son épouse ne fut pas épargnée et fut châtiée, car elle était mécréante.","explicationEn":"135. Except for his wife, because she was a woman whom the punishment of her people included within it, due to her being a disbeliever like them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037135","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-134.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-136.html"},{"numVerset":136,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْآخَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous détruisîmes les autres","tradEn":"Then We destroyed the others.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous anéantîmes ceux de son peuple qui l’ont traité de menteur et ne crurent pas en ce qu’il apportait.","explicationEn":"136. Then, I destroyed the remainder of his people who rejected him and did not believe in what he had brought.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037136","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-135.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-137.html"},{"numVerset":137,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّونَ عَلَيْهِمْ مُصْبِحِينَ","tradPropre":"Et vous passez certainement auprès d'eux le matin","tradEn":"And indeed, you pass by them in the morning","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Vous, les païens de la Mecque, au cours de vos voyages vers la Grande Syrie.","explicationUnanime":"Ô habitants de la Mecque, vous passez certainement près de leurs demeures de bon matin lorsque vous voyagez en Syrie.","explicationEn":"137. O people of Makkah! Indeed, you pass by their dwellings in you journeys towards the Levant in the morning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037137","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-136.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-138.html"},{"numVerset":138,"texteArabe":"وَبِاللَّيْلِ  أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ","tradPropre":"et la nuit. Ne raisonnez-vous donc pas?","tradEn":"And at night. Then will you not use reason?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Vous passez également à proximité de ces demeures de nuit. Ne raisonnez-vous pas et déduisez-vous pas d’enseignement du sort qu’ils connurent après avoir traité de menteur leur messager, avoir mécru et avoir commis une turpitude que personne n’avait commise avant eux?","explicationEn":"138. And likewise, you also pass by them at night. So do you not understand and take heed from the outcome of these people after they rejected, disbelieved and committed indecency, indecent behaviour, immorality, immoral behaviour, sexual indecency, sexual immortality which was unprecedented?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037138","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-137.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-139.html"},{"numVerset":139,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Jonas était certes, du nombre des Messagers.","tradEn":"And indeed, Jonah was among the messengers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Notre serviteur Jonas était du nombre des messagers d’Allah chargés d’annoncer la bonne nouvelle à leur peuple et de les avertir.","explicationEn":"139. And indeed, Jonah was one of the messengers of Allah who were sent to their people as bearers of good news and warners.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037139","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-138.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-140.html"},{"numVerset":140,"texteArabe":"إِذْ أَبَقَ إِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُونِ","tradPropre":"Quand il s'enfuit vers le bateau comble,","tradEn":"[Mention] when he ran away to the laden ship.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Son peuple qui avait rejeté son message.","explicationUnanime":"Il s’enfuit de son peuple sans la permission de son Seigneur et il embarqua à bord d’un navire plein de passagers et de marchandise.","explicationEn":"140. Remember when he became angry over his people and left them, boarding a ship full of passengers and goods.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037140","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-139.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-141.html"},{"numVerset":141,"texteArabe":"فَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِينَ","tradPropre":"Il prit part au tirage au sort qui le désigna pour être jeté [à la mer].","tradEn":"And he drew lots and was among the losers.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Pour être jeté à la mer afin d’alléger l’embarcation qui menaçait de sombrer.","explicationUnanime":"Chargé comme il était, le navire manqua de couler et les passagers tirèrent au sort afin de jeter à la mer certains d’entre eux. Ce fut lui que le sort désigna et il fut alors jeté à la mer.","explicationEn":"141. The ship was close to sinking because of its load, so the passengers drew lots to throw some of them overboard, fearing its sinking because of too many passengers. Jonah was one of the names that were drawn, and so they threw him in to the sea.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037141","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-140.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-142.html"},{"numVerset":142,"texteArabe":"فَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Le poisson l'avala alors qu'il était blâmable.","tradEn":"Then the fish swallowed him, while he was blameworthy.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Avoir quitté son peuple sans l’autorisation d’Allah.","explicationUnanime":"Après avoir été jeté à la mer, un poisson se saisit de lui et l’avala. Il commit assurément un acte blâmable en partant en mer sans la permission de son Seigneur.","explicationEn":"142. So when they threw him into the sea, a whale took him and swallowed him. He was to face the blame that was to come to him, because of him going to the sea without permission from his Lord.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037142","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-141.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-143.html"},{"numVerset":143,"texteArabe":"فَلَوْلَا أَنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِينَ","tradPropre":"S'il n'avait pas été parmi ceux qui glorifient Allah,","tradEn":"And had he not been of those who exalt Allāh,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si Jonas n’avait été du nombre de ceux qui évoquaient abondamment Allah avant de subir cette épreuve et s’il n’avait pas proclamé la gloire d’Allah dans le ventre du poisson,","explicationEn":"143. Had it not been that Jonah was one of those who would remember Allah abundantly before whatever afflicted him, and had it not been for his glorifying Allah in the stomach of the whale","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037143","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-142.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-144.html"},{"numVerset":144,"texteArabe":"لَلَبِثَ فِي بَطْنِهِ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ","tradPropre":"il serait demeuré dans son ventre jusqu'au jour où l'on sera ressuscité.","tradEn":"He would have remained inside its belly until the Day they are resurrected.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"il serait resté dans son ventre jusqu’au Jour de la Résurrection et lui aurait servi de tombe.","explicationEn":"144. he would have remained in the stomach of the whale until the Day of Judgement, with it having become his grave.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037144","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-143.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-145.html"},{"numVerset":145,"texteArabe":"۞ فَنَبَذْنَاهُ بِالْعَرَاءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Nous le jetâmes sur la terre nue, indisposé qu'il était.","tradEn":"But We threw him onto the open shore while he was ill.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous le jetâmes ensuite du ventre du poisson sur une terre dépourvue d’arbres et de construction. Il était alors amaigri suite à son long séjour dans le ventre du poisson.","explicationEn":"145. So I took him from the stomach of the whale and placed him on a land barren of trees and buildings, in the state that he was physically weak because of having stayed in the stomach of the whale for a while.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037145","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-144.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-146.html"},{"numVerset":146,"texteArabe":"وَأَنْبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِنْ يَقْطِينٍ","tradPropre":"Et Nous fîmes pousser au-dessus de lui un plant de courge,","tradEn":"And We caused to grow over him a gourd vine.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous fîmes pousser sur cette terre, au-dessus de lui, un plant de courge sous lequel il pouvait s’abriter et manger de ses fruits.","explicationEn":"146. I then made a gourd tree grow for him on that barren earth, which would give him shade.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037146","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-145.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-147.html"},{"numVerset":147,"texteArabe":"وَأَرْسَلْنَاهُ إِلَىٰ مِائَةِ أَلْفٍ أَوْ يَزِيدُونَ","tradPropre":"et l'envoyâmes ensuite (comme prophète) vers cent mille hommes ou plus.","tradEn":"And We sent him to [his people of] a hundred thousand or more.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le peuple qu’il avait fui, selon certains exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Après cela, Nous l’envoyâmes à son peuple qui comptait cent mille personnes ou plus.","explicationEn":"147. And I sent him back to his people, their number being a hundred thousand and more.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037147","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-146.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-148.html"},{"numVerset":148,"texteArabe":"فَآمَنُوا فَمَتَّعْنَاهُمْ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"Ils crurent, et nous leur donnâmes jouissance de la vie pour un temps.","tradEn":"And they believed, so We gave them enjoyment [of life] for a time.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils eurent la foi et crurent en ce qu’il leur apportait. Allah leur donna alors les moyens de jouir de leur vie ici-bas jusqu’à ce que les durées assignées à leurs vies se soient écoulées.","explicationEn":"148. They brought faith and believed in whatever He brought, so Allah granted them enjoyment in their worldly lives until their fixed lifetimes expired.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037148","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-147.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-149.html"},{"numVerset":149,"texteArabe":"فَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ أَلِرَبِّكَ الْبَنَاتُ وَلَهُمُ الْبَنُونَ","tradPropre":"Pose-leur donc la question: «Ton Seigneur aurait-Il des filles et eux des fils?","tradEn":"So inquire of them, [O Muḥammad], \"Does your Lord have daughters while they have sons?","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les païens affirmaient que les anges étaient les « filles d’Allah ».","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, pose la question suivante aux polythéistes sur un ton de réprobation: Attribuez-vous à Allah des filles alors que vous détestez en avoir et que vous vous attribuez des fils? Quelle est donc cette répartition?","explicationEn":"149. O Muhammad! So ask these idolaters, idolaters a rebuking question: “Do you attribute for Allah daughters which you yourselves dislike, while attributing sons for yourselves whom you love? What kind of distribution is this?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037149","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-148.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-150.html"},{"numVerset":150,"texteArabe":"أَمْ خَلَقْنَا الْمَلَائِكَةَ إِنَاثًا وَهُمْ شَاهِدُونَ","tradPropre":"Ou bien avons-Nous créé des Anges de sexe féminin, et en sont-ils témoins?».","tradEn":"Or did We create the angels as females while they were witnesses?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Comment prétendent-ils que les anges sont des femelles alors qu’ils n’étaient pas présents lors de leur création ni n’en ont été témoins?","explicationEn":"150. How could they claim the angels are female when they were not present at the time of their creation and did not witness it?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037150","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-149.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-151.html"},{"numVerset":151,"texteArabe":"أَلَا إِنَّهُمْ مِنْ إِفْكِهِمْ لَيَقُولُونَ","tradPropre":"Certes, ils disent dans leur mensonge:","tradEn":"Unquestionably, it is out of their [invented] falsehood that they say,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les mécréants mentent sur Allah et inventent sur Lui des faussetés","explicationEn":"151. Listen carefully! Indeed, the idolaters, idolaters from their attributing lies unto Allah","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037151","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-150.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-152.html"},{"numVerset":152,"texteArabe":"وَلَدَ اللَّهُ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ","tradPropre":"«Allah a engendré» mais ce sont certainement des menteurs!","tradEn":"\"Allāh has begotten,\" and indeed, they are liars.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"lorsqu’ils Lui attribuent une progéniture et ils mentent certainement lorsqu’ils prétendent cela.","explicationEn":"152. attribute offspring to Him, and indeed, they are liars in this claim of theirs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037152","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-151.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-153.html"},{"numVerset":153,"texteArabe":"أَصْطَفَى الْبَنَاتِ عَلَى الْبَنِينَ","tradPropre":"Aurait-Il choisi des filles de préférence à des fils?","tradEn":"Has He chosen daughters over sons?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah a-t-il choisi d’avoir une progéniture femelle que vous détestez au lieu d’une progéniture mâle que vous désirez? Certainement pas.","explicationEn":"153. Would Allah prefer daughters for Himself which you dislike, over sons which you like? Never!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037153","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-152.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-154.html"},{"numVerset":154,"texteArabe":"مَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ","tradPropre":"Qu'avez-vous donc à juger ainsi?","tradEn":"What is [wrong] with you? How do you make judgement?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô polythéistes, comment jugez-vous ainsi injustement en attribuant des filles à Allah tandis que vous vous attribuez des fils?","explicationEn":"154. O idolaters, what is wrong with you that you make this unjust judgment where you make daughters for Allah and sons for yourself?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037154","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-153.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-155.html"},{"numVerset":155,"texteArabe":"أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ne réfléchissez-vous donc pas?","tradEn":"Then will you not be reminded?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne réfléchissez-vous donc pas sur la fausseté de votre croyance corrompue? Si cela était le cas, vous n’auriez pas proféré ces allégations.","explicationEn":"155. Would you not take admonition of this wrong belief you are on? If you were to take heed, you would stop saying such as statement.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037155","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-154.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-156.html"},{"numVerset":156,"texteArabe":"أَمْ لَكُمْ سُلْطَانٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"Ou avez-vous un argument évident?","tradEn":"Or do you have a clear authority?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ou alors, détenez-vous un argument clair issu d’un livre ou apporté par un messager?","explicationEn":"156. Or do you have a clear proof from a divine scripture or a messenger from Allah?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037156","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-155.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-157.html"},{"numVerset":157,"texteArabe":"فَأْتُوا بِكِتَابِكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صَادِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Apportez donc votre Livre si vous êtes véridiques!»","tradEn":"Then produce your scripture, if you should be truthful.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Apportez donc le livre contenant votre argument si vous êtes véridiques dans ce que vous prétendez?","explicationEn":"157. Then bring your book which bears for you evidence of this if you are true in what you claim.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037157","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-156.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-158.html"},{"numVerset":158,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلُوا بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَ الْجِنَّةِ نَسَبًا  وَلَقَدْ عَلِمَتِ الْجِنَّةُ إِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et ils ont établi entre Lui et les djinns une parenté, alors que les djinns savent bien qu'ils [les mécréants] vont être emmenés (pour le châtiment).","tradEn":"And they have made [i.e., claimed] between Him and the jinn a lineage, but the jinn have already known that they [who made such claims] will be brought [to punishment].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> De parenté, précisent certains commentateurs. Selon d’autres, les païens ont établi un lien entre le Seigneur et les djinns en associant ces derniers à Son culte. Précisons néanmoins que, selon la majorité des exégètes, le terme « djinns » désigne ici - la seule fois dans le Coran - les anges présentés par les païens comme les « filles d’Allah ».","explicationUnanime":"Les polythéistes ont inventé un lien de parenté entre Allah et les anges qu’ils ne peuvent pas voir, en prétendant qu’ils sont les filles d’Allah. Or les anges savent qu’Allah mènera les polythéistes à leur châtiment.","explicationEn":"158. And the idolaters made blood ties between Allah and the angels when they claimed the angels are Allah’s daughters and their mothers are the elite jinns. But the jinns already know Allah will bring them to be reckoned, so if there was lineage between Him and them he would not bring them for that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037158","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-157.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-159.html"},{"numVerset":159,"texteArabe":"سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ","tradPropre":"Gloire à Allah. Il est au-dessus de ce qu'ils décrivent!","tradEn":"Exalted is Allāh above what they describe,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Qu’Allah soit sanctifié et élevé au-dessus de ce que Lui attribuent les polythéistes comme progéniture, associé et autres attributs qui ne Lui conviennent pas.","explicationEn":"159. Pure is Allah and exalted from what the idolaters describe Him with of that which does not befit Him, such as children, partners.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037159","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-158.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-160.html"},{"numVerset":160,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"Exception faite des serviteurs élus d'Allah.","tradEn":"Except the chosen servants of Allāh [who do not share in that sin].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Seuls les serviteurs élus d’Allah ne Lui attribuent que ce qui est majestueux et parfait.","explicationEn":"160. Except Allah’s chosen servants, as they do not describe Allah except with the qualities of majesty and perfection which are befitting for Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037160","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-159.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-161.html"},{"numVerset":161,"texteArabe":"فَإِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُونَ","tradPropre":"En vérité, vous et tout ce que vous adorez,","tradEn":"So indeed, you [disbelievers] and whatever you worship,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô polythéistes, vous et ce que vous adorez en dehors d’Allah","explicationEn":"161. So you, O idolaters, and what you worship besides Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037161","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-160.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-162.html"},{"numVerset":162,"texteArabe":"مَا أَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ بِفَاتِنِينَ","tradPropre":"ne pourrez tenter [personne],","tradEn":"You cannot tempt [anyone] away from Him","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"n’égarerez personne de la religion de vérité.","explicationEn":"162. You cannot misguide anyone from the true religion.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037162","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-161.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-163.html"},{"numVerset":163,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا مَنْ هُوَ صَالِ الْجَحِيمِ","tradPropre":"excepté celui qui sera brûlé dans la Fournaise.","tradEn":"Except he who is to [enter and] burn in the Hellfire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Sauf ceux qu’Allah a décrété qu’ils seront les gens de l’Enfer. Allah exécutera alors Son décret et ils seront mécréants puis iront en Enfer. Quant à vous et vos divinités, vous n’avez pas le pouvoir d’émettre un tel décret et de l’exécuter.","explicationEn":"163. Except one whom Allah has decreed is from the people of hell, as Allah will carry out His decree regarding him and so he will disbelieve and enter the fire. As for you and your gods, you do not have power over that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037163","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-162.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-164.html"},{"numVerset":164,"texteArabe":"وَمَا مِنَّا إِلَّا لَهُ مَقَامٌ مَعْلُومٌ","tradPropre":"Il n'y en a pas un, parmi nous, qui n'ait une place connue;","tradEn":"[The angels say], \"There is not among us any except that he has a known position.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Au ciel. Ou : qui ne se voit confier une tâche déterminée. Ces paroles sont prononcées par les anges.","explicationUnanime":"Les anges dirent, en guise d’affirmation de leur servitude à Allah et de désaveu de ce que prétendent les polythéistes: Il n’existe pas un ange parmi nous dont le mérite dans son adoration et son obéissance à Allah ne soit pas connu.","explicationEn":"164. And the angels said, stating their servitude to Allah and their being free of what the idolaters claimed: “There is nobody amongst us except that he has a known position in Allah’s worship and obedience.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037164","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-163.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-165.html"},{"numVerset":165,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الصَّافُّونَ","tradPropre":"nous sommes certes, les rangés en rangs;","tradEn":"And indeed, we are those who line up [for prayer].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous autres les anges sommes disposés en rangs lorsque nous adorons Allah et Lui obéissons et nous excluons qu’Allah détienne les attributs et les caractéristiques qui ne Lui conviennent pas.","explicationEn":"166. And we declare Him pure of qualities and descriptions which do not befit Him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037165","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-164.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-166.html"},{"numVerset":166,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْمُسَبِّحُونَ","tradPropre":"et c'est nous certes, qui célébrons la gloire [d'Allah].","tradEn":"And indeed, we are those who exalt Allāh.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous autres les anges sommes disposés en rangs lorsque nous adorons Allah et Lui obéissons et nous excluons qu’Allah détienne les attributs et les caractéristiques qui ne Lui conviennent pas.","explicationEn":"166. And we declare Him pure of qualities and descriptions which do not befit Him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037166","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-165.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-167.html"},{"numVerset":167,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ كَانُوا لَيَقُولُونَ","tradPropre":"Même s'ils disaient:","tradEn":"And indeed, they [i.e., the disbelievers] used to say,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants polythéistes de la Mecque disaient avant que Muħammad ne soit envoyé comme Messager:*Si nous avions un livre semblable à celui des anciens, comme la Torah par exemple,*nous aurions adoré sincèrement Allah.Or ils mentent lorsqu’ils disent cela car lorsque Muħammad leur apporta le Coran, ils mécrurent en lui. Ils sauront alors ce qui les attend comme châtiment terrible le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"167-170. And the idolaters from the people of Makkah used to say before Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sent: “If we had a book of the previous people, such as the Torah for example, we would have worshipped Allah sincerely”. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad (peace be upon him) brought them the Qur’ān but they disbelieved in it. So soon they will know the severe punishment that is waiting for them on the day of judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037167","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-166.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-168.html"},{"numVerset":168,"texteArabe":"لَوْ أَنَّ عِنْدَنَا ذِكْرًا مِنَ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"«Si nous avions eu un Rappel de [nos] ancêtres,","tradEn":"\"If we had a message from [those of] the former peoples,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants polythéistes de la Mecque disaient avant que Muħammad ne soit envoyé comme Messager:*Si nous avions un livre semblable à celui des anciens, comme la Torah par exemple,*nous aurions adoré sincèrement Allah.Or ils mentent lorsqu’ils disent cela car lorsque Muħammad leur apporta le Coran, ils mécrurent en lui. Ils sauront alors ce qui les attend comme châtiment terrible le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"167-170. And the idolaters from the people of Makkah used to say before Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sent: “If we had a book of the previous people, such as the Torah for example, we would have worshipped Allah sincerely”. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad (peace be upon him) brought them the Qur’ān but they disbelieved in it. So soon they will know the severe punishment that is waiting for them on the day of judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037168","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-167.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-169.html"},{"numVerset":169,"texteArabe":"لَكُنَّا عِبَادَ اللَّهِ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"nous aurions été certes les serviteurs élus d'Allah!","tradEn":"We would have been the chosen servants of Allāh.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants polythéistes de la Mecque disaient avant que Muħammad ne soit envoyé comme Messager:*Si nous avions un livre semblable à celui des anciens, comme la Torah par exemple,*nous aurions adoré sincèrement Allah.Or ils mentent lorsqu’ils disent cela car lorsque Muħammad leur apporta le Coran, ils mécrurent en lui. Ils sauront alors ce qui les attend comme châtiment terrible le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"167-170. And the idolaters from the people of Makkah used to say before Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sent: “If we had a book of the previous people, such as the Torah for example, we would have worshipped Allah sincerely”. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad (peace be upon him) brought them the Qur’ān but they disbelieved in it. So soon they will know the severe punishment that is waiting for them on the day of judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037169","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-168.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-170.html"},{"numVerset":170,"texteArabe":"فَكَفَرُوا بِهِ  فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils y ont mécru et ils sauront bientôt.","tradEn":"But they disbelieved in it, so they are going to know.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants polythéistes de la Mecque disaient avant que Muħammad ne soit envoyé comme Messager:*Si nous avions un livre semblable à celui des anciens, comme la Torah par exemple,*nous aurions adoré sincèrement Allah.Or ils mentent lorsqu’ils disent cela car lorsque Muħammad leur apporta le Coran, ils mécrurent en lui. Ils sauront alors ce qui les attend comme châtiment terrible le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"167-170. And the idolaters from the people of Makkah used to say before Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sent: “If we had a book of the previous people, such as the Torah for example, we would have worshipped Allah sincerely”. But they are lying in that, as Muhammad (peace be upon him) brought them the Qur’ān but they disbelieved in it. So soon they will know the severe punishment that is waiting for them on the day of judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037170","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-169.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-171.html"},{"numVerset":171,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ سَبَقَتْ كَلِمَتُنَا لِعِبَادِنَا الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"En effet, Notre Parole a déjà été donnée à Nos serviteurs, les Messagers,","tradEn":"And Our word [i.e., decree] has already preceded for Our servants, the messengers,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Notre Parole qui ne peut être contestée, a déjà décrété que Nos messagers seront secourus contre leurs ennemis par l’argument et la force accordée par Allah et que la victoire sera du lot de Nos soldats qui combattent pour la cause d’Allah afin que la parole d’Allah soit la plus haute.","explicationEn":"173. And victory is for My army which fights in My way, so that My word is the highest.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037171","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-170.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-172.html"},{"numVerset":172,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُمْ لَهُمُ الْمَنْصُورُونَ","tradPropre":"que ce sont eux qui seront secourus,","tradEn":"[That] indeed, they would be those given victory","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Notre Parole qui ne peut être contestée, a déjà décrété que Nos messagers seront secourus contre leurs ennemis par l’argument et la force accordée par Allah et que la victoire sera du lot de Nos soldats qui combattent pour la cause d’Allah afin que la parole d’Allah soit la plus haute.","explicationEn":"173. And victory is for My army which fights in My way, so that My word is the highest.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037172","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-171.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-173.html"},{"numVerset":173,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ جُنْدَنَا لَهُمُ الْغَالِبُونَ","tradPropre":"et que Nos soldats auront le dessus.","tradEn":"And [that] indeed, Our soldiers [i.e., the believers] will be those who overcome.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Notre Parole qui ne peut être contestée, a déjà décrété que Nos messagers seront secourus contre leurs ennemis par l’argument et la force accordée par Allah et que la victoire sera du lot de Nos soldats qui combattent pour la cause d’Allah afin que la parole d’Allah soit la plus haute.","explicationEn":"173. And victory is for My army which fights in My way, so that My word is the highest.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037173","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-172.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-174.html"},{"numVerset":174,"texteArabe":"فَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"Eloigne-toi d'eux, jusqu'à un certain temps;","tradEn":"So, [O Muḥammad], leave them for a time.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, détourne-toi de ces polythéistes obstinés pendant durée que seul Allah connaît, jusqu’à ce que le moment de les châtier arrive.","explicationEn":"174. So turn away, O Messenger, from these stubborn idolaters until a time which Allah knows, until the time of their punishment comes.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037174","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-173.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-175.html"},{"numVerset":175,"texteArabe":"وَأَبْصِرْهُمْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُونَ","tradPropre":"et observe-les: ils verront bientôt!","tradEn":"And see [what will befall] them, for they are going to see.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Regarde-les lorsque le châtiment s’abattra sur eux et eux-mêmes verront, même si cette vue ne leur sera d’aucune utilité.","explicationEn":"175. And look at them when the punishment comes upon them, for they themselves will see when seeing will not benefit.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037175","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-174.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-176.html"},{"numVerset":176,"texteArabe":"أَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Quoi! est-ce Notre châtiment qu'ils cherchent à hâter?","tradEn":"Then for Our punishment are they impatient?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces polythéistes veulent-ils hâter le châtiment d’Allah?","explicationEn":"176. Then do these idolaters hastily seek the punishment of Allah?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037176","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-175.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-177.html"},{"numVerset":177,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا نَزَلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ فَسَاءَ صَبَاحُ الْمُنْذَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Quand il tombera dans leur place, ce sera alors un mauvais matin pour ceux qu'on a avertis!","tradEn":"But when it descends in their territory, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque le châtiment d’Allah s’abattra sur eux un matin, ce sera certainement un mauvais matin pour eux.","explicationEn":"177. Then when Allah’s punishment comes upon them, what a bad morning will theirs be!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037177","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-176.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-178.html"},{"numVerset":178,"texteArabe":"وَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ","tradPropre":"Et éloigne-toi d'eux jusqu'à un certain temps;","tradEn":"And leave them for a time.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, détourne-toi d’eux jusqu’à ce qu’Allah décide de les châtier.","explicationEn":"178. And turn away, O Messenger, from them when Allah decides their punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037178","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-177.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-179.html"},{"numVerset":179,"texteArabe":"وَأَبْصِرْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُونَ","tradPropre":"et observe; ils verront bientôt!","tradEn":"And see, for they are going to see.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis observe et eux-mêmes verront le châtiment et la punition d’Allah s’abattre sur eux.","explicationEn":"179. And look, for these people will see the punishment and punishment of Allah that comes upon them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037179","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-178.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-180.html"},{"numVerset":180,"texteArabe":"سُبْحَانَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ الْعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ","tradPropre":"Gloire à ton Seigneur, le Seigneur de la puissance. Il est au-dessus de ce qu'ils décrivent!","tradEn":"Exalted is your Lord, the Lord of might, above what they describe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Muħammad, que ton Seigneur, le Seigneur de la force, soit sanctifié et élevé au-dessus des attributs péjoratifs dont L'affublent les polythéistes.","explicationEn":"180. O Muhammad, exhalt your Lord declaring his glorification, the Lord of Honour, and exalt Him above the qualities of deficiency the idolaters describe Him with.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037180","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-179.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-181.html"},{"numVerset":181,"texteArabe":"وَسَلَامٌ عَلَى الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et paix sur les Messagers,","tradEn":"And peace upon the messengers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que la salutation et l’éloge d’Allah soient sur Ses nobles messagers.","explicationEn":"181. And Allah’s greetings and His praise be for His noble messengers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037181","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-180.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-37-verset-182.html"},{"numVerset":182,"texteArabe":"وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"et louange à Allah, Seigneur des mondes!","tradEn":"And praise to Allāh, Lord of the worlds.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que l’éloge soit tout entier à Allah car Lui seul le mérite. Il est le Seigneur de tous les mondes, qui n’ont pas d’autre seigneur que Lui.","explicationEn":"182. And all praise is for Allah, as He is deserving of it, and He is Lord of all the creation. They have no lord besides Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"037182","lienPrecedent":"sourate-37-verset-181.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-38-verset-1.html"}]};